## Core Principles

1. **Type safety** — TypeScript strict, Zod, tRPC
2. **User scoping** — Every query filtered by authenticated `userId`; encrypt integration secrets
3. **Module boundaries** — No cross-feature imports; credit-cards is one feature among others
4. **Services own logic** — Routers thin; SOA/reminder/cron logic in `server/services/`
5. **Docs sync** — Update `application-inventory.md` when adding routes, routers, or tables
6. **Theme** — Light/dark via CSS variables (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`)
7. **Minimal UI copy** — No unsolicited descriptions or helper paragraphs; add text only when the user asks (see `.cursor/rules/21-minimal-ui-copy.mdc`)

## Architecture (summary)

```
app/ → features/dashboard/{credit-cards,reminders,automations,...} → shared
server/routers → server/services → lib/db
```

- `src/app/` = routes only (no business logic)
- Port legacy CLI from `pay-credit-cards/src/` into services—preserve behavior unless product changes

## Stack Commands

Use **Bun** (not npm): `bun install`, `bun run dev`, `bun run db:generate`, etc.

## When Working on Legacy CLI

If editing `automated-tasks/pay-credit-cards/`, follow `.cursor/rules/20-legacy-cli-reference.mdc`—do not apply crypto-trading rules.

